{
  "title": "India sets targets for green hydrogen use by some industries",
  "publication_date": "2023-01-13T00:00:00Z",
  "summary": "India has established mandatory green hydrogen consumption targets for various industries as part of its strategy to achieve net-zero emissions by 2070. The government's initiative aims to create demand for cleaner fuel alternatives.",
  "content": "By Sarita Chaganti Singh and Nidhi Verma\n\nNEW DELHI - India has introduced new requirements for specific industries to incorporate green hydrogen into their operations, marking a significant step in the country's commitment to reaching net-zero emissions by 2070. The government's initiative targets key industrial sectors to drive the adoption of cleaner fuel alternatives and reduce dependency on fossil fuels.\n\nThe move is part of India's broader strategy to transition towards renewable energy sources and decrease its carbon footprint. Green hydrogen, produced using renewable energy, is seen as a crucial element in the nation's sustainable energy future.",
