  "markdown_content": "## Policy Implementation\\n\\nIndia has introduced new requirements for specific industries to incorporate green hydrogen into their operations, marking a significant step in the country's commitment to reaching net-zero emissions by 2070. The government's initiative targets key industrial sectors to drive the adoption of cleaner fuel alternatives and reduce dependency on fossil fuels.\\n\\n## Strategic Focus\\n\\nThe move is part of India's broader strategy to transition towards renewable energy sources and decrease its carbon footprint. Green hydrogen, produced using renewable energy, is seen as a crucial element in the nation's sustainable energy future.",
